Invalid texture sizes don't crash the texture cache (warecomp STATUS.md
round 9).

On D3D12 the texture upload thread crashed (plume::setObjectName on a null
object, from TextureCache::uploadThreadLoop): a texture was created at a
size D3D12 refuses, then named. queueGPUUploadTMEM now keeps a decoded
texture's size between 1 and 8192, and the S2DEX object rectangle (0024)
skips sprites whose image size is under one texel or has the top bit set
(Worms Armageddon sends some, e.g. a negative width).

--- a/src/gbi/rt64_gbi_s2dex.cpp
+++ b/src/gbi/rt64_gbi_s2dex.cpp
--- a/src/gbi/rt64_gbi_s2dex.cpp
+++ b/src/gbi/rt64_gbi_s2dex.cpp
@@ -565,6 +565,13 @@
             RDP *rdp = state->rdp.get();
             const uint32_t renderMode = state->rsp->objRenderMode;
 
+            // Nothing sensible to draw for a size under one texel or with the top bit set
+            // (1024 texels or more, past what TMEM can hold): skip it rather than asking for
+            // a texture of that size.
+            if (((sprite.imageW >> 5) == 0) || ((sprite.imageH >> 5) == 0) || (sprite.imageW & 0x8000) || (sprite.imageH & 0x8000)) {
+                return;
+            }
+
             // Texels (imageW and imageH are u10.5).
             const int32_t texW = std::max<int32_t>(sprite.imageW >> 5, 1);
             const int32_t texH = std::max<int32_t>(sprite.imageH >> 5, 1);
--- a/src/render/rt64_texture_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/render/rt64_texture_cache.cpp
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 
 #define STB_IMAGE_IMPLEMENTATION
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include "ddspp/ddspp.h"
 #include "stb/stb_image.h"
 #include "xxHash/xxh3.h"
@@ -1264,6 +1265,13 @@
         TextureUpload newUpload;
         newUpload.hash = hash;
         newUpload.creationFrame = creationFrame;
+        // A texture is created at this size when it's decoded: a size of zero or past what a GPU
+        // allows fails to create one (on D3D12 it then crashed naming it). Keep it in range.
+        if (decodeTMEM) {
+            width = std::clamp(width, 1, 8192);
+            height = std::clamp(height, 1, 8192);
+        }
+
         newUpload.width = width;
         newUpload.height = height;
         newUpload.tlut = tlut;
